        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 75-year-old female patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she exhibited significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. Clinical response was satisfactory, with improvement in respiratory function and oxygen saturation. She is discharged in stable condition and I recommend continuation of her inhaled maintenance therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
